WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.301 --> 00:00:02.968
(hip hop music)

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.500
- Hey everyone, my name is Jesse,

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.320
and today, I'm gonna
be testing four famous

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.810
celebrity brownie recipes, to see

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.443
which one is actually the best.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.440
I'll be testing recipes
from Gordon Ramsay,

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.930
Guy Fieri, Ayesha Curry,

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.020
and Posh Spice herself, Victoria Beckham.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.490
I measure out all the ingredients,

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.670
as the recipe states, to
level the playing field,

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.490
and I got three brownie
lovers in the office

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.190
to test them out in a blind taste test.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.580
- Did someone say, "Brownies?"

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.590
- So, which celebrity has
the best brownie recipe?

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:33.813
Let's get baking.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.340
Up first is Gordon Ramsay.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.720
He starts by combining butter

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.940
and sugar in a large
bowl, and beating that

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.240
with electric mixer until
it's nice and fluffy.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.990
To that, he adds melted chocolate,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.490
and beats it again to combine.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.740
It's kind of chunky, so
I gave it a few stirs.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.536
To that, add salt, vanilla extract,

00:00:48.536 --> 00:00:52.473
cocoa powder, and flour, and
mix that all up, until smooth.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.043
Add some eggs.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.653
Mix it again until it
gets nice and fudgey.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.130
Add some milk, if it needs to
be thinned out a little bit.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.490
And then you're gonna add a
shit ton of dried cherries.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.343
Seriously, a lot of dried cherries.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.570
Pour that into a lined baking tin.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.753
Smooth it out, so it bakes nice and even.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.000
And pop it in the oven.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.113
Once baked, put some edible glitter,

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.520
Pop Rocks, and sprinkles on top

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.970
because you know, regular
brownies aren't enough.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.170
- This is like a child's
imagination of space.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.883
It looks like a kid's brownie.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.903
- Oh God, it crunched.

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:27.968
- What the heck did I just bite into?

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.290
- Oh my God, is that Pop Rocks?

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.380
- Oh, that's really weird.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.440
There's something else in here.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.300
- This is cherry instead of chocolate?

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.133
That's good.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.798
Cherries in brownies are a 100% yes.

00:01:35.798 --> 00:01:36.693
- Ugh, the fruit.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.663
- It's pretty good.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:39.793
Just leave the cherries on the side.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.470
Otherwise, pretty freaking
delicious. (smacks lips)

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:43.880
- [Jesse] Guy Fieri starts by combining

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.723
cut rhubarb, water, and
sugar, in a large pot,

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.140
and cooking it down 'til it
turns into a nice compote.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.260
Meanwhile, you're gonna
combine chili powder,

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.300
salt, flour, cinnamon, and baking powder,

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.510
and sift that all, so
there is no chunks in it.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:58.810
Set that aside, then
combine butter, white sugar

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.580
and beat that together
with electric beaters

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:01.930
until it's nice and fluffy.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.660
Add some eggs, and continue beating it

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.060
until it gets even fluffier.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.970
Add rum, vanilla extract,
and then bring back

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:10.670
that compote you made, and
add melted chocolate to it.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.573
Stir it together.

00:02:11.573 --> 00:02:13.820
It'll look kinda weird,
but add it to the eggs,

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.267
and fold that in, until
it's nice and sweet.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:18.420
Add some flour, and fold it again

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.070
until it's nice, fudgy, and
looks like a nice batter.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.973
Add chocolate and walnuts,
and stir it once more.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.830
Bring in a pan that you
lined with parchment paper.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.080
Put it in there, and pop it in the oven.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:29.913
There you have it.

00:02:29.913 --> 00:02:31.630
Brownies, that'll take you
straight to Flavor Town.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.933
- The crust on top is beautiful.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:37.633
I can really figure out my life,
just looking at this crust.

00:02:41.162 --> 00:02:41.995
- Mmm!

00:02:43.912 --> 00:02:44.745
Yes!

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.800
- There's some kind of
like, cinnamon in it.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.810
It doesn't really taste like a brownie.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.470
And it doesn't have the
texture of a brownie.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.700
It's more of like, a cake.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.373
- You can hear how sticky,

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.157
and like, moist this
brownie is, just listen.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.480
- [Jesse] Up next, is Ayesha Curry,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.860
with her horchata brownies.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.250
She starts by combining
butter and chocolate chips

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.853
in a double boiler, so
it gets nice and melted.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.233
Take that off the heat, add white sugar,

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.403
brown sugar, give that a stir,

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:13.423
and add four eggs.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.163
Add salt, cinnamon, flour.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.113
Stir that up again, 'til
it's nice and fudgy.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.160
Then, add slivered
almonds, and fold that in.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:27.483
Pour it into a prepared pan.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.770
Smooth it out, and pop in the oven.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.170
As it's cooking, get
some rice milk reducing,

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.893
pour it into a bowl, add rum, cinnamon,

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.550
give it a stir, and add a shit ton of

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.450
powdered sugar to it, so it
turns into nice, glossy glaze.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.470
Take your brownies out.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.703
Pour that glaze over,

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.090
and smooth it out.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:49.060
It'll harden in a few
hours, and it's good to go.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.393
- This looks like a brownie
with lots of makeup.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.333
Gorgeous.

00:03:55.605 --> 00:03:56.438
- Mmm.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.370
- Ooh, I like this.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.240
Not your classic brownie,
but you still get

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.120
all the elements of a brownie in it.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.480
- I'm very confused,
because this tastes amazing.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.100
It just doesn't taste like a brownie.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.440
- Oh, I really like whatever's on top.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.430
It's like, reminds me of
like, an apple crumble.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.370
- I can't decide, I'm sorry.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.203
- This is pretty good.

00:04:10.203 --> 00:04:12.010
I wish she had some kind of crunch to it,

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.893
but as is, beautiful.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.033
- Thumbs up for this one.

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.050
- [Jesse] Victoria Beckham starts by

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.640
combining sugar, cocoa
powder, and melted butter

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.503
in a bowl, and stir in all together.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.570
Add vanilla extract, four eggs,

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:26.170
and give that a good stir
until it's nice and fudgy.

00:04:26.746 --> 00:04:29.143
Add some baking powder, salt, flour,

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.660
give it another good stir,
and the batter is it.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.320
Posh keeps it nice and simple.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.250
Bring your pan in.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.083
Pour it in.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.363
Spread it out, so it
bakes nice and evenly,

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.580
and pop it in the oven.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.310
Now, you're baking like Beckham.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.880
- This looks like the brownie I know.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:44.870
- If you asked me to make a brownie,

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:45.920
like, this is what I would make.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.380
- This is not very crunchy.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:48.580
It's just like (splats).

00:04:50.237 --> 00:04:51.070
- Mm-mm.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.010
I don't like this one.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:53.370
- It's definitely a little drier.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.370
- Whoever made this, are you on a diet?

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:56.203
What's up?

00:04:56.203 --> 00:04:57.373
I'm missing my butter.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.560
I'm missing my chunks of chocolate.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.010
- It's not chocolatey enough.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.870
- [Jesse] So, which celeb
has the best brownies?

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:03.703
Let's find out.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.420
- This is what you guys
have all been waiting for.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:07.863
The best celebrity brownie is number one.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:09.240
I never would have thought to put cherries

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.850
in a brownie, and it tasted really good,

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.760
'cause there's like, chocolate and fruit

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.523
as a mixture, is always great.

00:05:14.574 --> 00:05:16.853
Ah, Gordon Ramsay, of course!

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.660
- Out of these four brownies, I think

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:21.363
my favorite is number three.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.870
It had those elements
of a classic brownie.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.064
It was gooey, the flavors
developed within it.

00:05:28.064 --> 00:05:30.110
Ooh, I like that!

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.810
- My favorite is definitely number two.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.650
The combination between soft and crunch

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.433
was so amazing, and I'm always
looking forward to that.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.963
Totally see this being his creation.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.823
- [Director] Kevin, we need
you to be the tie breaker.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:43.743
- Who, me?

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.000
I really don't like this one.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.310
I like that one a lot.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:51.930
I thought I liked it for a second.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.530
Number two is definitely my favorite.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.330
I'm a new fan of Guy Fieri, I guess.

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:56.730
(triumphant horn music)

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:57.880
- [Jesse] So, there you have it.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.050
Guy Fieri has the best brownies.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.830
Which celebrity recipes would
